# Files a release tool writes, which it will rewrite in its own style on every
# release. Style-gating a generated file means every release pull request fails
# lint for a reason no human introduced and no human can fix for good.
#
# `.release-please-manifest.json` is the concrete case: prettier wants
# `{ ".": "0.2.0" }` and release-please writes `{".":"0.2.0"}`. The file was
# hand-formatted when it was added, so main passed and the first release pull
# request did not.
